A method to identify particular items quite easily
was recently proposed in a Japanese NetHack forum.
It utilizes the characteristic of artifacts which
they refuse being made by #name-ing.

Ex) If you have a gray stone, just try to #name it
as "Heart of Ahriman". If it resist the attempt and
your hand slips, the gray stone is a luckstone.

The same method is also applicable to identify
a helm of brilliance and an amulet of ESP.

This is apparently a bug, or at least an abuse, though.

